A||||0||thomas_l||Cool running||||3||
Z||000000||thomas_l||06-06-2001||09:52 AM||||Last weekend I was inspecting my a/c system (87 GT) thinking of diving into an upgrade and discovered a pretty simple problem that hadn't stranded me yet. It seems that large opening in the nose makes the condenser pretty vulnerable to fairly large objects flying off the road. Even though I had not had any overheating problems, I noticed that the coolant temp seemed to take longer to come down once I got moving than it should.<P>The fins on the bottom half of the condenser were folded over flat. Worse yet, prior to me coming along, my car sat in tranny repair purgatory for several months behind the shop it was left at. During the stay, some mud-daubers covered about another 1/2 sq foot of condenser with their nests.<P>Straightening the fins and scooping the mud-dauber nests off have made a 100% improvement. In heavy traffic the fan cycles much faster and the temp drops quick even when moving fairly slow.<P>Are your condenser fins shaped like a sail?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
